From k189. (1) perl/scripts/loaded-modules.pl points git at its fixture gitconfig through GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL, which git < 2.32 ignores (perl:5.40-bullseye has git 2.30.2), so on the build image its git source never resolves and the modules only that path loads are not seen. Today harmless (the 6 modules the bullseye build packs fewer than the host are host-optional), but the build image is where it counts. Fix as k189 did in verify-binary.sh: also write the gitconfig as $HOME/.gitconfig of the fixture home. (2) check-binary-libs.sh says "OpenSSL 3" in a comment; the bullseye build links OpenSSL 1.1.

2026-11-14 00:58 Reproduced (worker): with a guard added to loaded-modules.pl (die unless the git source's skills/remote-skill got installed), the unfixed script in k189-build2:deps (perl:5.40-bullseye deps, git 2.30.2) dies 'the git source did not resolve'. Found on the way: the END block's system('rm') clobbered $?, so any die after the temp dir exited 0 (rc=0 with empty stdout) - fixed with local $? (rc now non-zero). Fix: the fixture gitconfig is also written as $HOME/.gitconfig of the fixture home. With it, bullseye: rc=0, 171 modules; host (git 2.47.3): 177. The 6-module gap is unchanged by the fix (Class::XSAccessor, ::Heavy, Moo::HandleMoose::_TypeMap, URI::_idna, URI::_punycode, XString: host-optional), so the git path loads no module of its own today. check-binary-libs.sh comment: OpenSSL 1.1 in the bullseye image (ldd: libssl.so.1.1), 3 on Debian 12+ (host: libssl.so.3).

